54,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,1,talk,Minato,,"The candidates are Woodland Walk, Market Plaza, Sports Terraces, and Wetland Restoration. I think the Wetland one might be risky with the clay.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,May,,"Market Plaza is hard-surfaced, so it's cheaper to maintain. But the habitat fund won't pay for it!","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Shizue,,Woodland Walk reminds me of the dead trees on the avenue. I don't trust it.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Sports Terraces could use those youth league volunteers. That would take the pressure off our seven staff members.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Wetland Restoration solves the drainage and heat issues, but it might fight the people walking to the tram.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, if the Wetland plan uses boardwalks, maybe people can still get to the tram?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,May,,"@Victoria, but who pays for the courts? The habitat fund won't cover the Sports Terraces' surfacing.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minato, the overflow basin worked well. Maybe the Wetland plan is the most durable option?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@May, the city budget must cover the rest. But the volunteer support for sports is a huge operational win.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, sports courts don't help with the August heat or the drainage callouts. We need a functional landscape.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I like the idea of the Wetland, but I'm still scared of the slippage.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,May,,"I'm leaning toward Market Plaza. It's the most affordable to keep up long-term, even if the initial funding is tricky.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree with the Wetland Restoration. It's like the basin; it works with the land rather than against it.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I still think Sports Terraces is the most realistic for our current staffing levels.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,Wetland Restoration is the only one that addresses the actual environmental failures of the site.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'll go with the Wetland. It sounds the most interesting and helpful for the city.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,May,,I can't ignore the upkeep costs. I vote for Market Plaza.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"For durability and peace, I vote for Wetland Restoration.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"For the sake of the staff and volunteers, I vote for Sports Terraces.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,Logic dictates we fix the drainage and heat. I vote for Wetland Restoration.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
